# Cloudflare Pages/Workers static-asset hosting reads this file directly —
# security headers a <meta> tag can't fully express (frame-ancestors,
# most of CSP) or shouldn't (X-Frame-Options has no meta-tag equivalent
# at all). Scoped to every path.
#
# connect-src allows any https: destination rather than a fixed list —
# the sync feature deliberately lets a person type in any server address
# of their own choosing (see SyncPanel.tsx), so this can't be narrowed to
# specific hosts without breaking that; still meaningfully restricts to
# encrypted connections only, blocking plain http:.
#
# style-src needs 'unsafe-inline': a handful of components use React's
# inline `style` prop for small one-off layout tweaks. This is a real,
# accepted gap, not an oversight — inline *styles* can't execute code the
# way inline *scripts* can, which is why script-src below stays strict
# with no such allowance.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src https:; frame-ancestors 'none'
